@startuml Delete Class Post by Teacher
actor Teacher
participant ": DeleteConfirmModal " as DeleteConfirmModal
participant ": Router " as Router
participant ": PostController " as PostController
participant ": PostService " as PostService
participant ": PostRepository " as PostRepository
database Database

Teacher->DeleteConfirmModal: 1. Teacher clicks to Delete Post
    activate Teacher
    activate DeleteConfirmModal

DeleteConfirmModal->DeleteConfirmModal: 2. Render Delete Confirmation Modal

Teacher->DeleteConfirmModal: 3. Confirm Delete

DeleteConfirmModal->Router: 4. Send DELETE /api/post?id={id}
    deactivate DeleteConfirmModal
    activate Router

Router->PostController: 5. Route Request to Controller
    deactivate Router
    activate PostController

PostController->PostService: 6. Delete Post Request
    deactivate PostController
    activate PostService

PostService->PostRepository: 7. GetByIdAsync(postId)
    activate PostRepository
    PostRepository->Database: 8. Query Post by Id
    activate Database
    Database-->PostRepository: 9. Return Post
    deactivate Database
    PostRepository-->PostService: 10. Return Post entity
    deactivate PostRepository

PostService->PostService: 11. Validate Post exists

PostService->PostRepository: 12. DeleteSoft(postId)
    activate PostRepository
    PostRepository->Database: 13. UPDATE Post SET IsDeleted = true
    activate Database
    Database-->PostRepository: 14. Post Deleted Successfully
    deactivate Database
    PostRepository-->PostService: 15. Post Deleted
    deactivate PostRepository

PostService-->PostController: 16. Return Success
    deactivate PostService
    activate PostController

PostController-->Router: 17. Send Success Response
    activate Router
    deactivate PostController

Router-->DeleteConfirmModal: 18. Post Deleted Successfully
    activate DeleteConfirmModal
    deactivate Router

DeleteConfirmModal->DeleteConfirmModal: 19. Show Success Message and Close Modal

DeleteConfirmModal-->Teacher: 20. Show Updated Posts List
    deactivate DeleteConfirmModal
    deactivate Teacher
@enduml





